*** Final draft

Incorporate by gravity: structure before scene, scene before line. Do not touch
a line while a structural problem remains unresolved. Every large change can
create problems downstream: when you cut a character, restructure a stretch or
change a revelation, reread everything around it before moving on.

And when you are convinced it is as good as you can make it, now, with the skill
you have now, let it go. A finished imperfect story teaches more than an
unfinished perfect one.

